# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. `railway up` uploads the working copy
# rather than the committed blobs, so on Windows — where core.autocrlf
# rewrites checkouts to CRLF — a script that is LF in git still reaches the
# Linux container with carriage returns in it. /bin/sh then reads the \r as
# part of each command and the container crash-loops on startup.
*.sh text eol=lf
